01:55:03.515 --> 01:55:07.045
so it will be on iTunes, it will be on Amazon for purchase,

01:55:07.045 --> 01:55:11.595
it will be on Xbox and Roku and FireStick

01:55:11.595 --> 01:55:16.595
and Comcast and DirecTV, and all those places.

01:55:17.425 --> 01:55:22.425
So I'm optimistic that it'll find its way,

01:55:23.495 --> 01:55:28.355
it's not going to be in front of a couple hundred

01:55:28.355 --> 01:55:32.825
million subscribers with a subscription to Netflix,

01:55:32.825 --> 01:55:34.985
but it will make its way into the world.

01:55:34.985 --> 01:55:38.175
Yeah, it'll find its way and so the December 25th

01:55:38.175 --> 01:55:43.175
limited release, is before the year turns over,

01:55:43.405 --> 01:55:45.175
is for Oscar consideration, right?

01:55:45.175 --> 01:55:47.485
Isn't that still the thing, it has to premiere

01:55:47.485 --> 01:55:50.005
in a theatrical way before?

01:55:50.005 --> 01:55:51.135
That's my understanding, yes.

01:55:51.135 --> 01:55:51.968
Yeah, I think you're right

01:55:51.968 --> 01:55:53.455
and then it'll be available after that.

01:55:53.455 --> 01:55:58.455
January and luckily, our partnership with the,

01:55:59.825 --> 01:56:04.825
I guess they call it PVoD, paid on-demand, company vertical

01:56:04.975 --> 01:56:09.975
is for the longest time, I think it was a 45-day window.

01:56:10.775 --> 01:56:12.365
If you launched in a theater, you couldn't have it

01:56:12.365 --> 01:56:15.438
on-demand within 45 days, but with COVID,

01:56:16.725 --> 01:56:19.325
all of the rules are changing now, and so we're able

01:56:19.325 --> 01:56:23.345
to come into theaters on December 25 and be available

01:56:24.425 --> 01:56:28.435
for on-demand on January 8th.

01:56:28.435 --> 01:56:33.435
So, it's excited for the film to be seen

01:56:33.645 --> 01:56:37.468
'cause I really I just...

01:56:37.468 --> 01:56:39.265
Hatice Cengiz, Jamal's fiance,

01:56:39.265 --> 01:56:41.235
I mean, she's become like a sister to me,

01:56:41.235 --> 01:56:46.235
and for me, this film has gone so far beyond making a film.

01:56:46.955 --> 01:56:51.955
I just feel so personally connected to the story

01:56:51.955 --> 01:56:56.955
and as an activist, I'm still involved in this

01:56:57.725 --> 01:56:58.765
on a daily basis.

01:56:58.765 --> 01:57:01.085
Hatice came to Sundance, right?

01:57:01.085 --> 01:57:02.285
She came to Sundance, yeah.

01:57:02.285 --> 01:57:04.345
She's still living in Istanbul?

01:57:04.345 --> 01:57:09.248
She's in Istanbul, she got a place from Washington DC,

01:57:10.435 --> 01:57:13.845
was starting her foundation to seek justice for Jamal,

01:57:13.845 --> 01:57:16.319
and then COVID happened, and she went back to Istanbul

01:57:16.319 --> 01:57:19.225
and she's been there since.

01:57:19.225 --> 01:57:21.655
So, hopefully, on the other side of COVID,

01:57:21.655 --> 01:57:24.615
she'll come back to Washington and resume work,

01:57:24.615 --> 01:57:27.695
and hopefully, with the Biden administration,

01:57:27.695 --> 01:57:32.375
there'll be a much warmer reception to the advocacy

01:57:32.375 --> 01:57:34.838
and human rights work that she's seeking to do.

01:57:36.025 --> 01:57:39.945
Where does the UN sit with all of this?

01:57:39.945 --> 01:57:41.915
I mean, a big part of the narrative of the film

01:57:41.915 --> 01:57:46.155
is kind of their own sort of investigation

01:57:46.155 --> 01:57:49.575
into what occurred, and then Hatice's testimony

01:57:49.575 --> 01:57:53.125
before the Council, but what is their power

01:57:53.125 --> 01:57:55.565
to do anything and kind of where do they sit

01:57:55.565 --> 01:57:57.095
with the whole affair?

01:57:57.095 --> 01:58:00.295
Well, this was a another kind of "Icarus" analogy,

01:58:00.295 --> 01:58:05.295
if I could make, is I had always viewed

01:58:05.575 --> 01:58:10.205
that the World Anti-Doping Agency had authority,

01:58:10.205 --> 01:58:13.845
and what I came to understand is that their job

01:58:13.845 --> 01:58:18.385
is basically to just observe and report and be lame duck

01:58:18.385 --> 01:58:20.015
and that they basically can't do anything.

01:58:20.015 --> 01:58:22.515
They're just the security guard in the neighborhood

01:58:22.515 --> 01:58:25.075
who drives around but is kind of feckless.

01:58:25.075 --> 01:58:25.908
Exactly.

01:58:25.908 --> 01:58:27.432
They're the guys like, go like,

01:58:27.432 --> 01:58:30.575
"Okay, these guys are cheating, but yeah,

01:58:30.575 --> 01:58:33.135
we have no power to punish them."

01:58:33.135 --> 01:58:37.028
And so that was the amazing thing that I saw,

01:58:38.545 --> 01:58:41.015
In "Icarus" in the story of Rodchenkov and this cheating,

01:58:41.015 --> 01:58:45.175
is okay, you have this global regulator of world sport,

01:58:45.175 --> 01:58:48.925
that also has no power to actually really do anything

01:58:48.925 --> 01:58:51.615
and enact punishment, and that the power is actually

01:58:51.615 --> 01:58:53.745
within the sporting federations themselves,

01:58:53.745 --> 01:58:55.925
and within the Olympics, and this, that, the other,

01:58:55.925 --> 01:58:58.445
and that WADA is really just the guy out there,

01:58:58.445 --> 01:59:00.635
is like the watchdog pointing a finger,

01:59:00.635 --> 01:59:03.175
but they're like a mall cop, right?

01:59:03.175 --> 01:59:06.355
Well, I've found this same thing to be the case

01:59:06.355 --> 01:59:07.725
with the UN.

01:59:07.725 --> 01:59:12.725
So in the film, you see Agnes Callamard,

01:59:15.575 --> 01:59:18.925
who is a special repertoire of United Nations.

01:59:18.925 --> 01:59:19.885
She's a character.

01:59:19.885 --> 01:59:22.995
An investigator, she's French, but she also teaches

01:59:22.995 --> 01:59:27.235
at Columbia, and so, on the outset, you go,

01:59:27.235 --> 01:59:32.235
okay, Agnes, is the UN, she's actually not,

01:59:33.035 --> 01:59:35.975
she's a special repertoire to the United Nations,

01:59:35.975 --> 01:59:40.095
meaning that she has been given permission

01:59:40.095 --> 01:59:44.315
