02:45:08.885 --> 02:45:12.965
everything becomes a risk assessment.

02:45:12.965 --> 02:45:13.955
Yeah.

02:45:13.955 --> 02:45:18.658
Yeah, it's interesting, because the streaming universe,

02:45:19.685 --> 02:45:23.995
you do have to credit it with providing the opportunity

02:45:23.995 --> 02:45:28.835
for a lot of independent stories to be told and shared

02:45:28.835 --> 02:45:31.705
and celebrated in a way that would not have been possible

02:45:31.705 --> 02:45:33.745
in the theatrical window model.

02:45:33.745 --> 02:45:36.515
So it has done...

02:45:36.515 --> 02:45:39.615
Not as many people would have seen "Icarus",

02:45:39.615 --> 02:45:42.263
if it were not for Netflix, of course.

02:45:42.263 --> 02:45:46.075
It's like it's unbelievable, the power of these platforms

02:45:46.075 --> 02:45:49.845
to help smaller filmmakers and stories

02:45:49.845 --> 02:45:53.115
that aren't gonna get greenlit, to be in the multiplex,

02:45:53.115 --> 02:45:56.375
and yet at the same time, there is this risk analysis

02:45:56.375 --> 02:45:59.145
that is having this squelching impact.

02:45:59.145 --> 02:46:02.938
What you have is, like in the case of Netflix,

02:46:03.778 --> 02:46:08.665
the Netflix that did "Icarus" three years ago,

02:46:08.665 --> 02:46:11.838
is not the Netflix of today, it's a different company.

02:46:13.495 --> 02:46:16.135
That was a company that had 100 million subscribers

02:46:16.135 --> 02:46:18.979
versus 200 million subscribers.

02:46:18.979 --> 02:46:23.979
That was a company that was very hungry at the at the time

02:46:24.385 --> 02:46:28.245
to show that it could be an awards contender,

02:46:28.245 --> 02:46:33.245
show that it could evolve beyond "House of Cards"

02:46:36.931 --> 02:46:41.931
and it was it was a different company three years ago.

02:46:43.891 --> 02:46:46.635
And what happens, for better for worse,

02:46:46.635 --> 02:46:50.025
'cause I love Netflix, I mean the majority

02:46:50.025 --> 02:46:53.505
of "The Queens Gambit" that I just finished watching

02:46:53.505 --> 02:46:56.375
is extraordinary, it's extraordinary.

02:46:56.375 --> 02:46:59.525
And there's so much extraordinary content on there,

02:46:59.525 --> 02:47:04.525
and I am sure that I will continue to do content,

02:47:04.705 --> 02:47:08.555
make content and have content on Netflix.

02:47:08.555 --> 02:47:10.955
They're awesome, and they're amazing at what they do,

02:47:10.955 --> 02:47:12.165
I love them.

02:47:12.165 --> 02:47:16.482
But on the other hand, because of how big they are,

02:47:16.482 --> 02:47:19.155
and the growth that they've had and where they're at

02:47:19.155 --> 02:47:24.155
in the world right now, there is a whole other risk model

02:47:24.495 --> 02:47:28.785
that comes into it, and in many ways,

02:47:28.785 --> 02:47:32.835
you can't fault them either, because if you're running

02:47:32.835 --> 02:47:37.835
that company, the burden that comes on top of that, to grow,

02:47:41.615 --> 02:47:45.345
to have shareholder value, and to also not put your company

02:47:45.345 --> 02:47:48.475
at risk, also becomes very, very hard.

02:47:48.475 --> 02:47:50.615
And so I don't have that answer to it,

02:47:50.615 --> 02:47:55.615
because at the same time I'm not angry at them,

02:47:55.755 --> 02:47:57.782
I love them, I think they're amazing

02:47:57.782 --> 02:48:00.775
and I love what they're doing and I love the content

02:48:02.018 --> 02:48:05.005
and the forum that they've provided for so many people

02:48:05.005 --> 02:48:06.255
and what they did for "Icarus"

02:48:06.255 --> 02:48:08.698
was outstanding and astounding.

02:48:09.945 --> 02:48:13.335
At the same time, there's a conundrum where something

02:48:13.335 --> 02:48:18.335
gets so big, that risk assessment will always get in the way

02:48:19.505 --> 02:48:23.035
or become a variable as to whether you do something or not.

02:48:23.035 --> 02:48:23.868
Yeah.

